  "question": {
    "text": "A cell of emf <math><mi>E</mi></math> and internal resistance <math><mi>r</mi></math> supplies currents for the same time <math><mi>t</mi></math> through external resistance <math><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo></math>100 <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> separately. If the heat developed in both cases is the same, then the internal resistance of the cell is given by",
